- 3. That he is an elector of the municipality and is eligihle to vote in the election in which he is a candidate;

- 4. The name of the office which he is seeking;

Ss. That he is eligible to hold such office;

- 6. That he has never been convicted and sentenced in any court of competent jurisdiction for frauduient violation of primary or election laws, malfeasance in office, or felony involving moral turpitude under the laws of this state or any other state of the United States, or that his civil rights have been restored; and

- 7. That he will not knowingly violate any provision of this ordinance or any rules and regulations adopted by the governing authority of the Town of Pine Mountain.

